      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding\n\n**Yes—one component-issue event for manufacturing order `MO-25-09-1070` was created 75 minutes after September entered Pending Close. Its recorded `POSTED` status is inconsistent with Oracle’s documented treatment of newly created transactions.**\n\n| Item | Recorded value |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing/work order number | `MO-25-09-1070` |\n| Work order ID | `WO-2025-09-004` |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine–DeKoven / Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Cost period | `Sep-25` (`PER-COST-2025-09`) |\n| Cost event | `CE-250904-0004` — `INPUT` (component issue) |\n| Source transaction | `TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070` |\n| Amount | **USD $284,763.42** (`28,476,342` cents) |\n| Event-created time | **`2025-09-30T19:15:00`** |\n| Pending Close time | **`2025-09-30T18:00:00`** |\n| Time after Pending Close | **75 minutes (1 hour 15 minutes)** |\n| Recorded accounting status | **`POSTED`** |\n\n**Calculation:** `19:15:00 − 18:00:00 = 4,500 seconds ÷ 60 = 75 minutes`.\n\nThe timestamps above are reproduced exactly; the source does not specify a timezone.\n\n## Policy assessment\n\nOracle’s *Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting* documentation states that new transactions falling in the Pending Close period or an earlier period **“won’t be staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting”** and are processed after the period is closed or reopened. It specifically states that transactions created after the Pending Close date will not be processed.\n\nThe documented exceptions are revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments. This event is an **`INPUT` component issue**, not one of those exceptions. Accordingly, its recorded **`POSTED` status is not consistent with that policy**.\n\n**Sources:** `system/oracle_scm_cost_management/state.db`, tables `work_orders`, `cost_periods`, and `work_order_cost_events`; Oracle SCM Cost Management 26B policy PDF, “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” printed page **225** (PDF page **233**).\n\nThe review was read-only; no database records were changed.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
  ],
